# Problem Statement

## 1. Title

Event Ticketing & Seat Booking Platform


## 2. Domain

Event Management and Online Ticket Booking


## 3. Who is the User?

### 1. Customer

- View available events
- View event details
- Check available seats
- Book tickets
- View booking details


### 2. Event Admin

- Add and manage events
- Add and manage seats
- View customer bookings
- Monitor seat availability


## 4. What Problem Are We Solving?

Traditional event ticket booking can be time-consuming and may not provide accurate information about available seats. Customers may have difficulty finding events, checking seat availability, and reserving their preferred seats. There is also a risk of two customers trying to book the same seat. The proposed system provides a centralized platform where customers can view events, check real-time seat availability, and book tickets easily.


## 5. Proposed Solution

The Event Ticketing & Seat Booking Platform will be developed using Python with FastAPI. The application will allow users to view events, select available seats, and book tickets online. The system will store event, seat, and booking information in a database.

The application will provide:

- User registration and login
- Event listing and event details
- Seat availability checking
- Seat selection
- Ticket booking
- Booking history
- Booking cancellation
- Admin event management
- Admin seat management
- Booking management


## 6. Core Entities / Database Tables

The system will contain the following main database tables:


### Users

- User ID
- Name
- Email
- Password
- Role


### Events

- Event ID
- Event Name
- Description
- Venue
- Event Date
- Ticket Price


### Venues

- Venue ID
- Venue Name
- Location
- Capacity


### Seats

- Seat ID
- Venue ID
- Seat Number
- Seat Status


### Bookings

- Booking ID
- User ID
- Event ID
- Booking Date
- Total Amount
- Booking Status


### Booking Items

- Booking Item ID
- Booking ID
- Seat ID
- Seat Number


## 7. User Roles & Permissions

| Role | Permissions |
|---|---|
| Admin | Add events, manage seats, view bookings, manage event information |
| Customer | View events, check seats, book tickets, view bookings, cancel bookings |


## 8. Success Criteria

The project will be considered successful when:

- A customer can register and log in successfully.
- Customers can view available events.
- Customers can check available and booked seats.
- Customers can select and book available seats.
- The system prevents booking an already-booked seat.
- Customers can view their booking details.
- Customers can cancel a booking.
- Admins can add and manage events.
- Admins can manage seats.
- Booking information is correctly stored in the database.


## 9. Out of Scope

The following features will not be developed in this project:

- Online payment gateway
- Bank/refund processing
- QR-code scanning
- Live chat
- AI-based event recommendations
- Third-party ticket marketplace
- Facial recognition
- Advanced analytics


## 10. Chosen Track

**Python – FastAPI**

**Database:** SQLite

**Backend:** Python FastAPI

